The final column displays the maximum HP of the longest game.

This is all a bit odd because we have both speed attempts and farmers to
content with - and the average and median results may well reflect which
of those the class is best suited to, rather than anything else - and in
the tourney there was a definite incentive to play quickly in real time,
which would discourage using lots of game turns to a degree. However, this
still is not completely meaningless; I think we can deduce that there are
no glaring differences between the classes. 

Perhaps, BTW, my clock suggestions to Boudewijn ought to be adjusted when
the player is Fast or Very Fast - so that the clock would be based on
player moves as if not Burdened; that would avoid giving yet another
substantial advantage to fast classes and characters with speed boots.
Arguably this figure ought to be reported at game-end rather then the
current turn count; that would make fastest ascension less of a speed boot
gamble.

It looks to me as if 50,000 turns is not atypical.

