Of course we don't know these are farmers - except the 1,388, which I
happen to know is - but we can be pretty certain the 2,510 game was.

What about most turns? We had one 427K turn game, one 314K turn game
(finished with only 213 MHP, so likely not a farmer); one 160K, one 138K,
3 120-130K, 6 100-100K, and everything else sub-90K. These 13 are fewer
than 10% of the 168 ascensions. At the other end of the scale there are a
small number of ascensions sub-20K, but lots of 20-40K.

I would be inclined to say, then, that 20-30K is fast; 50K average; and
above 80K is slow. This would suggest that a midgame clock could start to
make its presence felt around the 40K mark - a fast player can avoid it
altogether, but would only start to mete out serious pain around 80-100K,
to either demand a finish or grind the player down to nothing. By this
time you hit 150K, anything goes.
